---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ConceptDiagram from "../components/ConceptDiagram.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Get started" description="Choose your path: browser learning, local kind cluster, or AWS hosting.">
  <section class="hero container prose">
    <h1>Get started</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This lab supports <strong>three modes</strong> that work together. Most people start in the browser,
      then spin up a real local cluster when they want hands-on muscle memory.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <ConceptDiagram />
  </section>

  <section class="container prose">
    <h2>Path A — Browser only (fastest)</h2>
    <p>No Docker daemon, no kubectl, no AWS. Learn concepts and practice simulated commands.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><code>cd kubernetes && make site-dev</code></li>
      <li>Open <a href="http://localhost:4321">http://localhost:4321</a></li>
      <li>Start with <a href="/docker.html">Docker fundamentals</a> → <a href="/learn.html">Kubernetes modules</a></li>
      <li>Debug scenarios on <a href="/troubleshoot.html">Troubleshoot</a></li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Path B — Local practice (recommended)</h2>
    <p>Real Docker and kind cluster on your machine.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Install <a href="https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Docker</a>, <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/tools/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kubectl</a>, and <a href="https://kind.sigs.k8s.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kind</a></li>
      <li><code>make docker-lab</code> — build and run the sample container</li>
      <li><code>make local-lab</code> — kind cluster for Kubernetes</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/Jacob-Idolor/Pet_Projects/tree/main/kubernetes/labs/lab-00-docker" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lab 00 — Docker</a> then Lab 01</li>
    </ol>
    <p>See <code>kubernetes/SETUP.md</code> in the repo for Docker Desktop K8s, minikube, and OpenShift alternatives.</p>

    <h2>Path C — Host on AWS (optional)</h2>
    <p>Deploy the learning website to S3 + CloudFront (~$1–5/month). This does <strong>not</strong> create EKS — only static hosting.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Set up AWS CLI profile and edit <code>infra/terraform/terraform.tfvars</code></li>
      <li><code>make aws-init && make aws-plan && make aws-apply</code></li>
      <li><code>make aws-deploy</code></li>
    </ol>
    <p>Full details: <code>kubernetes/infra/README.md</code></p>

    <h2>Suggested learning loop</h2>
    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong>Read</strong> Docker + a K8s module →
        <strong>Quiz</strong> →
        <strong>Simulate</strong> in browser →
        <strong>make docker-lab</strong> + <strong>make local-lab</strong> →
        <strong>Troubleshoot</strong> scenarios.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docker.html">Start with Docker</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/troubleshoot.html">Troubleshoot</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
